# Styling Conventions

## Architecture

Styles are split across co-located CSS files under `src/styles/`. `src/index.css` is the entry point and contains only three things: `@import` statements, `@theme` design tokens, and `@layer base` resets.

```
src/
  index.css                    ← imports, tokens, base resets
  styles/
    typography.css             ← type scale (type-display, type-title, type-eyebrow, etc.)
    shared.css                 ← reusable classes (content-column, nt-card, section-title, home-quote)
    crt-overlay.css            ← soft vignette only
    layout/
      header.css
      footer.css
      page-content.css
    sections/
      hero.css, demo.css, multicam.css, workflows.css, …
      content-page.css         ← SEO/content page shared styles
    ui/
      fade-in.css
```

## Adding New Styles

When adding a new section or component:
1. Create a new `.css` file in the appropriate directory (`sections/`, `layout/`, or top-level `styles/`)
2. Wrap all classes in `@layer components { ... }`
3. Add an `@import` for it in `src/index.css`
4. Use semantic class names that describe **what the element is**, not how it looks

## When to Use Inline Tailwind Utilities

Tailwind utility classes on JSX are fine for **simple one-off modifiers**. Rule of thumb: if you're combining 3+ layout/spacing utilities, create a named class in CSS instead.

## Typography Scale

Defined in `src/styles/typography.css`. Inter throughout. White headings; pink for eyebrows/accents; yellow reserved for small badges (e.g. "Save 20%").

| Class | Usage | Element |
|---|---|---|
| `type-display` | Hero heading | `<h1>` |
| `type-title` | Section / page title | `<h2>`, page `<h1>` |
| `type-eyebrow` | Small accent label above a title | `<span>` |
| `type-subtitle` | Hero descriptor | `<p>` |
| `type-body` | Body copy | `<p>`, `<li>` |
| `type-card-heading` | Card sub-heading | `<h3>` |
| `para-gap` | Paragraph bottom spacing | Any text element |

## Design Tokens

Defined in `src/index.css` under `@theme`. Always use tokens rather than raw values:

| Token | Utility class | Value |
|---|---|---|
| `--color-yellow` | `text-yellow`, `bg-yellow` | `#faff00` (accent only) |
| `--color-pink` | `text-pink`, `bg-pink` | `#ff008c` (primary CTA) |
| `--color-pink-hover` | `bg-pink-hover` | `#e6007d` |
| `--color-cyan` | `text-cyan` | `#2bffed` (focus rings) |
| `--color-bg` | `bg-bg` | `#000000` |
| `--color-border` | `border-border` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.18)` |
| `--color-white-60` | `text-white-60` | secondary text |
| `--font-sans` / `--font-heading` / `--font-body` | Inter |

Primary CTA colour is **pink**. Use the shared `Button` component for all CTAs. Use `.nt-card` for card surfaces.

## Pointer Events

Section containers often use `pointer-events: none` so overlays don't block the page. Interactive elements (images, buttons, links) use `pointer-events: auto`.

## No Inline Style Objects

Do not use React `style={{ }}` props for layout. All layout goes in CSS files.
